# PCManFM Flux

Based on tagged upstream PCManFM 1.4.0, Debian 1.4.0-1 packaging, and
Tomas M's desktop/browser/standalone improvements. Existing upstream
contributors and their Git history remain unchanged.

The source and installed package are named pcmanfm-flux; the binary remains
/usr/bin/pcmanfm, and the ordinary pcmanfm package is replaced. The versioned
virtual Provides on pcmanfm keeps dependencies on the original binary package
satisfiable; Conflicts/Replaces prevent two owners of the same paths.

Tomas M's patches are maintained as Debian quilt patches. At runtime,
pcmanfm-flux requires the matching MiniOS libfm4-flux and
libfm-gtk3-4-flux libraries rather than allowing an unpatched backend.
Its build dependencies use libfm-gtk3-dev-flux and its original installed
executable and desktop configuration paths are preserved.
The one Debian package source is built on Bionic with GTK3 and
debhelper 11; do not produce a separate Trixie binary set without an
explicit technical requirement. The libfm-flux GTK2 component is also
built for Bionic LXDE consumers from that same source package.
Runtime GdkPixbuf dependencies support both old and new package names.
